{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791377644,"nonce":"9HHUgLGc2MQmy7C1DcxnxVPgoYI=","title":"Infer abstract array reads from explicit accessors or instantiated storage","message":"At HEAD 315e544d93e2d823ad124bf73865ca960afe7d5f, ArrayAccess inference only follows typedefs and a method named get. An abstract over Array\u003cFloat\u003e otherwise produces Dynamic, so MIR reads an i64 slot and treats the raw Float bits as a Dynamic pointer. An unrelated helper get():String can also incorrectly determine the indexed value type. Explicit @:arrayAccess methods with another name lose their declared result type.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/regressions/AbstractArrayElements.hx. Native Haxe passes. The HEAD pinned Cranelift run fails the first check, \"underlying element over helper get\". The fixture also covers Slots\u003cFloat\u003e through a typedef, writes, Slots\u003cInt\u003e/Slots\u003cString\u003e, and a named @:arrayAccess read method returning Int instead of the storage's Float.\n\nChange: infer declared @:arrayAccess methods before following abstract storage. Instantiate storage using receiver generic arguments. Abstract annotations with underlying:None recover storage from the declaration, without changing their global representation. Ordinary class get behavior remains unchanged.\n\nThe first candidate fixed the concrete abstract but still crashed on Slots\u003cFloat\u003e at fault=0x400c000000000000 (3.5 bits), because the instantiated annotation had no underlying type. Resolving only the annotation's stored underlying is insufficient. The second candidate also resolves declaration storage; native and pinned Cranelift now pass the complete fixture.\n\nInitial full corpus candidate: 883 -\u003e 884 / 1094, Issue3247 PASS (5 checks), no lost passes. Issue3360 advances from CRASH to WRONG_ANSWER at its final HelperMacros.typeError assertion; its float array reads complete. TestIO remains failing with a classification change. Final candidate corpus verification follows in a comment.\n\nEvidence: /tmp/rayzor-abstract-array-{baseline,pinned-v1,pinned-v2,native-v1,mir-v1}.log; /tmp/rayzor-abstract-array-final-v1/report.tsv. The float crash is distinct from Dynamic iterators yielding raw array slots (a957716).","files":null}]}